@page
@{
    Layout = null;
}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Orbit Dock Keymaster | Mission Control</title>
    <style>
        :root { color-scheme: dark; font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; background: #090f20; color: #e9efff; }
        body { margin: 0; background: radial-gradient(ellipse at top right, #20365b, transparent 65%); min-height: 100vh; }
        main { max-width: 1000px; margin: auto; padding: 64px 24px; }
        .eyebrow { color: #9eeadd; letter-spacing: .18em; font-size: .8rem; font-weight: 700; }
        h1 { font-size: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 6rem); margin: 12px 0; letter-spacing: -.06em; }
        h2 { font-size: 1.3rem; }
        p { line-height: 1.7; color: #c6d1e8; max-width: 65ch; }
        .cards { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(240px, 1fr)); gap: 20px; margin: 40px 0; }
        article, aside { border: 1px solid #425570; border-radius: 18px; padding: 24px; background: #111c30; }
        .tag { color: #9eeadd; font-size: .85rem; }
        code { color: #e3c7ff; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
        footer { padding-top: 24px; color: #c6d1e8; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
    <div class="eyebrow">ORBIT DOCK KEYMASTER / FLIGHT 001</div>
    <h1>Orbit Dock Keymaster.</h1>
    <p>Different fleets. Different missions. Precisely scoped access.
        A hands-on exploration of multi-tenant authorization in .NET 10.</p>
    <section class="cards" aria-label="Engineering principles">
        <article><span class="tag">01 / FLEETS</span><h2>Boundaries first</h2>
            <p>Organizations are isolated application tenants. Selecting a fleet does not grant membership.</p></article>
        <article><span class="tag">02 / CLEARANCE</span><h2>Permissions are local</h2>
            <p>Viewer, Editor, and Admin belong to a fleet, not to a global identity.</p></article>
        <article><span class="tag">03 / FLIGHT CHECKS</span><h2>Evidence over promises</h2>
            <p>Relational tests check membership, forged claims, revocation, and cross-fleet reads.</p></article>
    </section>
    <aside aria-label="Current build limitations">
        <h2>Pre-launch checkpoint</h2>
        <p>This first build has protected read APIs and a synthetic local database.
            Real sign-in, mission editing, and audit history are not implemented.
            There is no demo login or browser identity bypass.</p>
        <p>Mission endpoint: <code>/api/organizations/{organizationId}/projects</code></p>
    </aside>
    <footer>Orbit Dock Keymaster is a learning project, not a production security guarantee.</footer>
</main>
</body>
</html>
